        253.98159790039062,
        322.4257507324219,
        302.438720703125,
        333.80413818359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pr.A1",
      "bbox": [
        227.7187042236328,
        335.3791198730469,
        249.4739990234375,
        344.1421813964844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "n =1/",
      "bbox": [
        246.48519897460938,
        335.0772705078125,
        267.55328369140625,
        346.45562744140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "= Pr.On =x/x=N",
      "bbox": [
        304.8804016113281,
        322.4256591796875,
        371.3244934082031,
        337.7761535644531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N\u0004",
      "bbox": [
        314.7831115722656,
        334.5113525390625,
        324.51165771484375,
        343.4777526855469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "x=1",
      "bbox": [
        314.3147888183594,
        351.55950927734375,
        324.9788513183594,
        357.60284423828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pr.On =x/x",
      "bbox": [
        328.2663879394531,
        341.23626708984375,
        373.14013671875,
        351.5475769042969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ";",
      "bbox": [
        374.3720703125,
        329.4642639160156,
        376.8019714355469,
        337.776123046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "thus it is easy to show that E.On|A1",
      "bbox": [
        48.089263916015625,
        363.1164245605469,
        190.8632049560547,
        372.5433349609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "n = 1/ = E.On/ + var.On/=E.On/. Hence we see the importance of",
      "bbox": [
        187.87440490722656,
        363.4780578613281,
        443.60137939453125,
        374.8564453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "choosing a resampling scheme that minimizes the variance of the number of times that each particle is",
      "bbox": [
        48.089111328125,
        374.19378662109375,
        443.607666015625,
        382.5056457519531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "resampled; or of not resampling every time step.",
      "bbox": [
        48.089111328125,
        384.1563415527344,
        229.99940490722656,
        392.46820068359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To illustrate this empirically, I considered a simple toy model X0 ∼N.0, 100/,",
      "bbox": [
        57.055511474609375,
        393.365966796875,
        349.7549743652344,
        403.6772766113281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Xn|xn−1 =Xn−1 ∼",
      "bbox": [
        127.82760620117188,
        414.5628662109375,
        192.7976837158203,
        424.8741760253906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0003",
      "bbox": [
        194.04312133789062,
        401.9399719238281,
        200.9562225341797,
        410.9063720703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N.xn−1, σ2/",
      "bbox": [
        202.25006103515625,
        409.7833251953125,
        246.59657287597656,
        419.92425537109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "with probability 0.99,",
      "bbox": [
        281.2669677734375,
        410.89813232421875,
        362.6739196777344,
        419.2099914550781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N.xn−1, 1/",
      "bbox": [
        202.24966430664062,
        420.1075134277344,
        242.12396240234375,
        429.886962890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "otherwise,",
      "bbox": [
        281.26678466796875,
        420.8607482910156,
        320.2168273925781,
        429.172607421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Yn|Xn =xn ∼N.xn, 1/:",
      "bbox": [
        202.54718017578125,
        434.03985595703125,
        286.328857421875,
        444.35125732421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We simulated data for σ = 0:1. Fig. 8(b) shows how the probability of sampling an independent path in",
      "bbox": [
        48.08979797363281,
        449.3526916503906,
        443.6022644042969,
        458.417724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the conditional SMC step depends on T, N and the type of resampling. Results are given for multinomial",
      "bbox": [
        48.08979797363281,
        460.06842041015625,
        443.6084289550781,
        468.3802795410156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "resampling and for stratiﬁed resampling (Kitagawa, 1996; Carpenter et al., 1999), which is known to",
      "bbox": [
        48.0906982421875,
        470.0309753417969,
        443.60595703125,
        478.34283447265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "minimize var.On/. We see that stratiﬁed sampling requires much smaller values of N to have the same",
      "bbox": [
        48.091583251953125,
        479.9935607910156,
        443.6028137207031,
        488.3056945800781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "performance as for multinomial sampling. Also, as pointed out in the paper, you want N to increase lin-",
      "bbox": [
        48.089508056640625,
        489.9563903808594,
        443.602783203125,
        498.26824951171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "early with T to have a roughly constant performance (this suggests that the central processor unit cost of",
      "bbox": [
        48.08953857421875,
        499.9189758300781,
        443.6106872558594,
        508.2308349609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SMC scales as O.T 2/; this sounds competitive with or better than standard MCMC sampling; see Roberts",
      "bbox": [
        48.090431213378906,
        508.76690673828125,
        443.6057434082031,
        518.193603515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(2009)).",
      "bbox": [
        48.08972930908203,
        519.8443603515625,
        77.40985107421875,
        528.1561889648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "I have two other comments on particle Gibbs sampling. Firstly it seems that how you initialize the con-",
      "bbox": [
        57.056129455566406,
        529.806884765625,
        443.6120910644531,
        538.1187133789062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ditional SMC update is important. Naive strategies of sampling particles from the prior will lead to many",
      "bbox": [
        48.08972930908203,
